From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hjviewer <haejin.cho@yonsei.ac.kr>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 06:48:03 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 139/160] hjviewer: Windows 11 snap layouts on the maximise
 button and the title bar's window menu (UX-K4)

UX-K4 (U44, design build/v19/design/u44.md with its review):
- runner: new hjv_caption.cpp/.h. HjvCaptionAttach(controller) is called after SetChildContent
  for the main window and in DesktopMultiWindowSetWindowCreatedCallback for each session window
  (no plugin fork). It registers a top-level window delegate
  (FlutterDesktopPluginRegistrarRegisterTopLevelWindowProcDelegate) and the "hjv/caption"
  channel; the Flutter view is subclassed only when Dart first sends the maximise button's box on
  Windows 11 (RtlGetVersion build >= 22000), so Windows 10 and the off option leave it alone.
  Over the box the view answers HTTRANSPARENT and the top-level window HTMAXBUTTON, unless the
  window lacks WS_CAPTION (full screen), WS_THICKFRAME (window_manager would answer HTNOWHERE
  first) or WS_MAXIMIZEBOX. Hover via TrackMouseEvent(TME_LEAVE | TME_NONCLIENT), DefWindowProc
  still called for WM_NCMOUSEMOVE; the click is armed on WM_NCLBUTTONDOWN/DBLCLK over the button,
  cleared on any WM_NCLBUTTONUP and on WM_NCMOUSELEAVE or another WM_NCMOUSEMOVE only while the
  left button is up, and a WM_NCLBUTTONUP on the button while armed is a click, as with Windows'
  own button. A new or removed box resets the look and the armed click. The state is a window
  property on both windows, freed (and the view's procedure put back) on the view's WM_NCDESTROY.
  showWindowMenu answers first, then shows the window's system menu at the cursor with its items
  set from IsZoomed and the style, and posts the chosen WM_SYSCOMMAND.
- Dart: new desktop/widgets/hjv_caption.dart (the box in physical pixels: localToGlobal x
  devicePixelRatio, edges rounded up, minus the top resize band measured from the view's top;
  re-sent on metrics changes; null on dispose or when the button cannot be clicked; the native
  hover and pressed states; the click runs the button's own onTap). tabbar_widget.dart: the
  maximise button is wrapped when the option allows, the bar's right-click opens the window
  menu, a right-click on a tab stays the tab's. Neither on the connection (cm) window nor on the
  install window (the install window is known by its process, see below).
- The local option hjv-snap-layouts ('N' off, 'Y' on, else kHjvSnapLayoutsDefault = true) is
  read in Dart once per window; the Windows gate (decisions.md) ships it off by flipping the
  default.
- Tests: flutter/test/hjv_caption_test.dart (pure).

UX-K4 (U44), review fixes: the install window:
- The install window got the bar's window menu and, on Windows 11, Windows' snap layouts on its
  maximise button: _hjvCaptionWindow tested DesktopTabType.install, but InstallPage builds its
  tabs as DesktopTabType.main and no page uses DesktopTabType.install. The window is now known by
  its process: the --install process is the only one that sets no desktopType (main.dart).
  New pure hjvCaptionWindow(desktopType?.name, cmTabs:) in hjv_caption.dart; tabbar_widget.dart
  calls it. InstallPage keeps DesktopTabType.main (its tab label and _saveFrame stay as they are).

UX-K4 (U44), review fixes: the window menu's own switch:
- New kHjvWindowMenuDefault (hjv_caption.dart), read where the bar's right-click opens the
  window menu: at the Windows gate either half (snap layouts, window menu) is one constant.

UX-K4 (U44), review fixes: the runner's hover tracking:
- SetMaxButton clears the TrackMouseEvent flag when the box goes: TopLevelProc skips messages
  while there is no box, so a WM_NCMOUSELEAVE then left the flag set and the next box's hover
  could stay grey after the pointer left.

Review-fix tests: hjv_caption_test.dart, three more (the window menu's switch, the connection and install
windows left out, the DesktopType names and the install branch read from the sources).

Lane snap commits ebdfcf0 and b3d6067, squashed on merge.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
